{"id": "EUVD-2017-19024", "enisaUuid": "4e4d8076-f2bc-3122-9981-d1d75da71e31", "description": "Javo Spot theme for WordPress before 3.0.0 contains a path traversal vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to read arbitrary files via the fn parameter of the jvfrm_spot_get_json AJAX action. Attackers can send GET requests to /wp-admin/admin-ajax.php with fn set to ../../wp-config.php to retrieve database credentials and secret keys. Exploitation evidence was first observed by the Shadowserver Foundation on 2023-10-19.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T10:57:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T10:57:22", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://codeseekah.com/2017/02/09/javo-themes-spot-lfi-vulnerability/", "https://wpscan.com/vulnerability/2d465fc4-d4fa-43bb-9c0d-71dcc3ee4eab", "https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/blob/main/http/vulnerabilities/wordpress/wp-javospot-lfi.yaml", "https://themeforest.net/item/javo-spot-multi-purpose-directory-wordpress-theme/13198068", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/javo-spot-wordpress-theme-3.0.0-path-traversal-via-admin-ajax-php-fn-parameter"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f9g9-m55p-h787", "CVE-2017-20287"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "51915d83-f926-3da2-8bd2-50c6294fb377", "product": {"name": "Javo Spot", "vendor": {"name": "Javo Themes"}}, "product_version": "0 <3.0.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "74c4d482-8c37-316b-8aef-58f35f73a512", "vendor": {"name": "Javo Themes"}}], "isExploited": false}